  "Id": 3475,
  "Title": "Visits at CIME Nairobi: Strengthening Partnerships and Collaboration",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "CIME recently hosted important visits with MP Shah Hospital and Linedata that underscore ongoing collaborations and potential partnerships.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClassC39BE5EE548D436B83ED12654CDB605F\"><p>\u200b</p><p>CIME Nairobi recently hosted important visits that underscore ongoing collaborations and potential partnerships. </p><p>Firstly, Sister Eunice Bett, Principal of the Nursing School at MP Shah Hospital, along with her colleagues, visited CIME to discuss a forthcoming Memorandum of Understanding between AKU and MP Shah Hospital. The collaboration will include the use of Visually Enhanced Mental Simulation (VEMS) as a cost-effective method for training non-technical skills.</p><p>In another visit, a delegation from Linedata, a global financial technology, services, and solutions provider, toured CIME Nairobi. Linedata has been a key sponsor of AKU's initiatives in Kampala. During their visit, they had an unexpected encounter with a simulated emergency scenario, where the team successfully revived a &quot;patient&quot; named Dan, in honor of one of the rescuers. This visit provided a glimpse into the kind of impactful work that will take place at the upcoming University Centre in Kampala.<br></p><p><br></p></div>",
